{"author":{"id":"8d2e0405f08ac6c481f912544d6d5c0f58b2dc14a7e51ad4d499ee7a34567943"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794222368,"nonce":"mwGzDMEmIzaK/DmQMamrsG7rPoY=","title":"jno.solve.rosenbrock() is refused by a nonlinear jno.fdm march with linear= set","message":"fdm.solve(time=jno.solve.rosenbrock(), linear=jno.solve.lu()) on a nonlinear transient (a 2-D Brusselator) raises: 'this scheme is linearly implicit ... so nonlinear= has nothing to drive. Drop nonlinear='. The caller passed no nonlinear=; _run_block fills it in (newton(direct=True)) before the scheme sees it, so Rosenbrock cannot be used from jno.fdm on a nonlinear problem with an assembled step solve.","files":null}]}